new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e04dfa8b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc-build/md061.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+This rule is triggered when a heading's level is greater than the maximum
+heading level allowed by the `maximum` parameter:
+
+```markdown
+# Heading
+
+## Heading
+
+#### Heading
+```
+
+To fix this, restructure the document so headings are no deeper than the
+maximum level (for example, with `maximum` set to `3`):
+
+```markdown
+# Heading
+
+## Heading
+
+### Heading
+```
+
+Note: With the default value of `6`, this rule never reports a violation.
+
+Rationale: Deeply nested headings can be a sign that a document should be
+split into smaller documents or restructured.
